ll began March 25, 2019.  Owners may contact customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Acura's recall number for this recall is P3W.  Honda's recall number for this recall is N3X.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":437032,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=19V060000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":11,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2016","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD"},{"year":"2015","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2015","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD"},{"year":"2016","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2017","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2016","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2017","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"17V418000","received":"2017-06-29","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"ELECTRICAL SYSTEM:12V/24V/48V BATTERY","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2013-2016 Honda Accord vehicles.  The case for the battery sensor, part of the battery management system, may allow water to get in, potentially causing an electrical short.","consequence":"An electrical short increases the risk of a fire.","remedy":"Honda will notify owners, and dealers will replace the sensor, free of charge.  Dealers will perform an interim remedy of applying adhesive to the case to prevent water intrusion.  The recall began November 8, 2017.  Owners may contact American Honda Customer Support Center at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's number for this recall is KG0.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":1148550,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=17V418000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":4,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2014","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD"},{"year":"2013","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD"},{"year":"2016","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD"},{"year":"2015","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"23V858000","received":"2023-12-19","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"FUEL SYSTEM, GASOLINE:DELIVERY:FUEL PUMP","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2013-2023 Honda Accord, Civic Coupe, Civic Sedan, Civic Hatchback, Civic Type R, CR-V, HR-V, Ridgeline, Odyssey, Acura ILX, MDX, MDX Hybrid, RDX, RLX, TLX, 2019-2022 Honda Insight, Passport, 2020 Honda CR-V Hybrid, 2018-2019 Honda Clarity PHEV, Fit, and 2015-2020 Honda Accord Hybrid, Pilot, Acura NSX vehicles.  The fuel pump inside the fuel tank may fail.","consequence":"Fuel pump failure can cause an engine stall while driving, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the fuel pump module, free of charge.  Owner letters were mailed September 6, 2024.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's numbers for this recall are KGC and KGD.  This recall is an expansion of NHTSA recall numbers 21V-215 and 20V-314.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":2490460,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=23V858000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":107,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"RDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"ILX"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"NSX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"RDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"FIT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"ILX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"NSX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true},{"campaign":"26V332000","received":"2026-05-22","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"AIR BAGS:SENSOR:OCCUPANT CLASSIFICATION:FRONT PASSENGER","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2018-2021, 2023 Acura TLX, 2019-2024 RDX, 2017-2020, 2022-2026 MDX, 2017-2021, 2023, 2025 Honda Ridgeline, 2017-2022 Pilot, 2019-2021 Passport, 2018-2026 Odyssey, 2019-2022 Insight, 2019-2021 HR-V, 2018-2020 Fit, 2020-2022 CR-V Hybrid, 2017-2022 CR-V, 2017-2018, 2021 Civic Type R, 2017-2021 Civic hatchback, 2016-2020 Civic coupe, 2016-2022 Civic, 2017-2022 Accord Hybrid, and 2016-2022 Accord vehicles. The front passenger seat weight sensor may crack and short circuit, which can cause the air bags to deploy unintentionally during a crash.","consequence":"Air bags that deploy unintentionally during a crash increase the risk of injury.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the seat weight sensors, free of charge. Owner notification letters were mailed July 7, 2026. Owners may contact Honda's customer service at 1-888-234-2138. Honda's numbers for this recall are BOL, WO9, OOA, WOM, XOH, NOC, POD, BOE, UOF, POB, EOG, AOI, QO8, TOJ, DO7, and SOK. This recall expands previous NHTSA recall number 24V064. Vehicle Identification Numbers (VINs) involved in this recall will be searchable on NHTSA.gov beginning May 29, 2026.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":98892,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=26V332000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":92,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD HYBRID"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V HYBRID"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2021","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC"},{"year":"2021","make":"ACURA","model":"RDX"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V"},{"year":"2022","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC TYPE R"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC TYPE R"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD HYBRID"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true}]}
